{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_019r2a5eWq2aGSa1kf8hKAR1", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n2\t\n3\timport requests\n4\timport structlog\n5\t\n6\tlog = structlog.get_logger()\n7\t\n8\tLEDGER_URL = \"https://ledger.internal.acme.example/v1/postings\"\n9\t\n10\t\n11\t@dataclass\n12\tclass Invoice:\n13\t    id: str\n14\t    customer_id: str\n15\t    subtotal_cents: int\n16\t    tax_cents: int = 0\n17\t    ledger_ref: str | None = None\n18\t    lines: list = field(default_factory=list)\n19\t\n20\t\n21\tdef finalize(invoice):\n22\t    resp = requests.post(LEDGER_URL, json={\"invoice\": invoice.id, \"amount\": invoice.subtotal_cents + invoice.tax_cents}, timeout=10)\n23\t    resp.raise_for_status()\n24\t    invoice.ledger_ref = resp.json()[\"ref\"]\n25\t    log.info(\"invoice_finalized\", invoice_id=invoice.id)\n26\t    return invoice\n27\t\n28\t\n29\tdef finalize_once(invoice):\n30\t    if invoice.ledger_ref:\n31\t        return invoice\n32\t    return finalize(invoice)\n33\t"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0d658e43-8ff4-4c78-b207-e0d9c2461559", "uuid": "a5796be8-8ff1-4152-b082-31187d10b112", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T15:49:40.625Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/tmp/mte-pq-finalize-us00tdoq/ledgerline/src/billing/invoices.py", "content": "from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\nimport requests\nimport structlog\n\nlog = structlog.get_logger()\n\nLEDGER_URL = \"https://ledger.internal.acme.example/v1/postings\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Invoice:\n    id: str\n    customer_id: str\n    subtotal_cents: int\n    tax_cents: int = 0\n    ledger_ref: str | None = None\n    lines: list = field(default_factory=list)\n\n\ndef finalize(invoice):\n    resp = requests.post(LEDGER_URL, json={\"invoice\": invoice.id, \"amount\": invoice.subtotal_cents + invoice.tax_cents}, timeout=10)\n    resp.raise_for_status()\n    invoice.ledger_ref = resp.json()[\"ref\"]\n    log.info(\"invoice_finalized\", invoice_id=invoice.id)\n    return invoice\n\n\ndef finalize_once(invoice):\n    if invoice.ledger_ref:\n        return invoice\n    return finalize(invoice)\n", "numLines": 33, "startLine": 1, "totalLines": 33}}}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbnJSAYnz62pEY7voNib", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The main thing to know is that `finalize()` is not idempotent. The code in `src/billing/invoices.py` matches the stored hazard memory.\n\n- **Double-posting:** `finalize()` (line 21) POSTs to the external ledger with no idempotency key. Each call creates a new posting, and `ledger_ref` is only set after the response comes back.\n- **Use `finalize_once()`:** it returns early if `invoice.ledger_ref` is already set, and otherwise calls `finalize()`. Call it from new code.\n- **Don't add retries around `finalize()`:** the request has a 10-second timeout. If the ledger commits the posting but the response is lost, `ledger_ref` stays unset. A retry, or even a second `finalize_once()`, would then double-post.\n- **`finalize_once()` isn't concurrency-safe either:** it checks `ledger_ref` in memory with no lock. Two workers finalizing the same invoice at once could both pass the check and post twice.\n- **Fixing the timeout gap:** that needs a ledger-side idempotency key, for example one derived from `invoice.id`. That depends on whether the ledger API supports it, which I haven't checked.\n\nI only searched for `finalize` and read `invoices.py`, so I haven't looked at the callers or the tests. Nothing in the code contradicts the stored memory, and I haven't saved anything new."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 545, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25224, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 545}, "output_tokens": 458, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0d658e43-8ff4-4c78-b207-e0d9c2461559", "uuid": "6